# Every text file is stored with LF line endings and checked out with LF, so
# that Prettier and the generated-code check behave the same on Windows, macOS
# and CI. .editorconfig already asks for LF; without this file, git's
# core.autocrlf setting rewrites the working tree to CRLF on Windows and the
# formatting check fails on a clean checkout.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
